## RDRPOSTagger and the GPL

This code is MIT-licensed, so GPL-3.0 sources are neither vendored nor imported at
runtime. `wrappers/rdrpos.py` implements the SCRDR inference procedure itself from the
published algorithm (Nguyen et al.). The implementation was checked for fidelity against the
upstream tagger on the full EWT test split, with the authors' published model (trained on
UD_English-EWT r2.4): **0 differences across all 25 094 words**. That model is not part of
the plan and is not downloaded.

The plan's `rdr_ewt` is retrained on the EWT train split with the authors' own learner.
`scripts/train_rdrpos.py` downloads the learner (GPL-3.0-or-later) from the official
repository at a pinned commit, checks each of its files against a recorded SHA-256, keeps it
outside this repository (by default in `~/.cache/rdrpostagger/`) and runs it there as a
separate program; nothing of it is imported or vendored. The `.RDR` and `.DICT` files it
writes are derived from UD_English-EWT train (CC BY-SA 4.0), stay in the ignored
`model_cache/rdrpos_ewt/` and are not redistributed. `wrappers/rdrpos.py` reads them with its
own reader, which tags all 25 147 words of the EWT dev split as the learner's own tagger does.

If the thesis cites this tagger, cite the software as GPL-3.0-or-later and credit its authors,
Nguyen, Nguyen, Pham & Pham (2013-2019). That range dates the software, not a paper: the method
is cited by the two papers `wrappers/rdrpos.py` names (2014 and 2016).

